// Starburst: fireworks over a hilltop town, built from free particles and light.
//
// Every shell is a ring of hot star material painted in the air at the top of
// its rocket and blown apart in the same tick by one explosion at its center.
// An explosion in the air throws each cell straight out from its center as a
// free particle with a fixed-point velocity, so the ring opens as a round
// burst; the blast's flash lights the town for a moment and its fire leaves a
// puff of smoke. The stars arc and fall under real gravity (9.84 m/s^2) and
// cool in flight, and their colour is their temperature: molten metal stars
// leave white-gold, fade through orange to a dull red and freeze to scrap;
// molten glass stars burn pale yellow and shatter to glittering shards; lava
// stars glow orange, dim to red and freeze to rubble. Their light, summed over the whole
// burst, falls on the roofs below. Spent stars land cold, so the town is
// intact at the end. Rockets are flame painted at each rocket's head as it
// climbs, leaning downwind; the flames then burn out and their smoke drifts in
// the wind (3). Timeline: quiet night, a white-gold shell from behind the keep
// (2.3 s), silver and red shells left and right (6-14 s), a crescendo in three
// colours (14-21 s), one large double-break shell over the keep (25.7 s) whose
// stars shower and light the roofs, then the smoke drifts off and the town
// returns to torchlight. The event lines are generated by a script.
[scene]
name = starburst
description = Fireworks over a hilltop town: rings of molten metal, glass and lava burst into free particles that cool from white-gold through orange to red in flight and light the roofs below.
bounds = 0 -760 960 100
seed = 0x5b57
wind = 3
ticks = 2100

